                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6339e43-fe7b-4fe6-97a8-5d5de2166011",
                                                "sense_id": "328241ea-2b40-3917-a294-ffb07b86036a",
                                                "text": "I lay, as it were, in the Paphian bower of bliss, in a state of exquisite sensations quite impossible to describe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6104a815-dbec-42bf-9fb1-6e86282c7bff",
                                                "sense_id": "328241ea-2b40-3917-a294-ffb07b86036a",
                                                "text": "People passed, but they held me not. Paphian eyes rayed upon me, and left me unscathed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8545b167-72d5-3fff-b3fa-d1c2ec68fc66",
                                        "entry_id": "ef090e65-17b2-318a-9f2e-cd4e28577ab3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to Paphos, the mythical birthplace of the goddess of love on the island of Cyprus."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb5bf334-45b7-4e7d-815a-fb372d6ff8d9",
                                                "sense_id": "8545b167-72d5-3fff-b3fa-d1c2ec68fc66",
                                                "text": "Then thus incensed, the Paphian queen replies: / \"Obey the power from whom thy glories rise: / Should Venus leave thee, every charm must fly, / Fade from thy cheek, and languish in thy eye. / Cease to provoke me, lest I make thee more / The world’s aversion, than their love before; / Now the bright prize for which mankind engage, / Than, the sad victim, of the public rage.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d08c86d-1822-4141-a235-c9fc3c237a35",
                                                "sense_id": "8545b167-72d5-3fff-b3fa-d1c2ec68fc66",
                                                "text": "So ſaying, the might of Vulcan loos’d the ſnare, / And they, detain’d by thoſe coercive bands / No longer, from the couch upſtarting, flew, / Mars into Thrace, and to her Paphian home / The Queen of ſmiles, where deep in myrtle groves / Her incenſe-breathing altar ſtands embow’r’d."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Paphian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9ee11d00-8d74-3765-a3d0-c3121bc17a4c",
                                        "entry_id": "6b31997a-86fc-39e9-b54b-f7be72c30569",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A prostitute."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literary"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "873d586a-6dfc-4eb8-a699-805f137b55e3",
                                                "sense_id": "9ee11d00-8d74-3765-a3d0-c3121bc17a4c",
                                                "text": "They reach'd the hotel: forth stream'd from the front door / A tide of well-clad waiters, and around / The mob stood, and as usual several score / Of those pedestrian Paphians who abound / In decent London when the daylight's o'er; / Commodious but immoral, they are found / Useful, like Malthus, in promoting marriage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec870385-ec68-49da-9dbc-67de22ed8922",
                                                "sense_id": "9ee11d00-8d74-3765-a3d0-c3121bc17a4c",
                                                "text": "A smile I had learned to know elsewhere lurked at one corner of my paphian's mouth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "342d7cbb-2a8a-3861-be7d-a21baa83617e",
                                        "entry_id": "6b31997a-86fc-39e9-b54b-f7be72c30569",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A resident of Paphos."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f5a737a9-6bcd-4fbd-8a2b-6e02b29a56a3",
                                                "sense_id": "342d7cbb-2a8a-3861-be7d-a21baa83617e",
                                                "text": "Then there is the mastus. Apollodorus the Cyrenæan, as Pamphilus says, states that this is a name given to drinking-cups by the Paphians."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
